Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||08-31-99||08:58 PM||||When I do eventually get my Fiero ('86 SE 2M6 4spd.) running, I am going to need a new muffler, for my car backfired due to the timing being way off, and blew a hole the size of my fist in the muffler. What kind of muffler should I replace it with? I am looking for good sound quality, and decent flow. I was wondering if i should pick up a pair of glasspacks and run the exhaust straight from the headers out the glasspacks... I am 17 and this is my testosterone mobile.. BTW, I am in CA so smog and stuff is pretty strict.
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-31-99||09:45 PM||||STETZ, you might want to replace the cat. as well. Many companys make free-flow converters. Iam finding out that the best muffler, (price, sound & flow) is the Flow Master. A good muffler shop can make this work. Summit & Jeg`s has the mufflers & cat.
Z||000002||Dale||09-01-99||12:00 AM||||Definatly a good choice.  You really dont want to just run glasspacks, you need some back pressure in the pipe unless your going to run the car at 5000rpm all the time.
